# M10.4 acceptance: selection and find in Single Page on tests/data/slides-16x9.pdf
# (8 slides, 960 x 540 pt; slide N has "Slide N" in large type and the body line
# "Point <word>: distinct body text for slide N.", see tests/data/make_slides_pdf.py).
# Run through tests/acceptance/m10.4.sh, which builds the clipboard reader and writes
# the expected clipboard texts. Each `run .../clipcheck <name>` compares the clipboard
# with its expected text byte for byte.
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent (the implementer conforms or files a
# TEST DISPUTE):
#   - A drag selects from the word under the press to the word under the release, in
#     reading order, as in M3.2. Double-click selects the word under the pointer.
#   - A selection is drawn only on the page it belongs to. Flipping does not clear it.
#   - Ctrl+C copies the selection while another slide is shown.
#   - In Single Page, Enter and Shift+Enter in the find field (and the bar's Next and
#     Previous buttons) flip to the slide holding the match, and wrap at both ends.
#   - Typing a query may or may not flip to its first match. The steps only judge the
#     slide shown after typing when the first match is on the slide already shown.
#
# Geometry at the default 1400x900 window, as in m10.3.steps: Single Page at 76%, the
# slide at x 237..968, y 267..677 with the find bar closed. The pane moves down by the
# bar's height (about 40 px) while the bar is open. The body line is centred at
# y 505. Word centres from pdftotext -bbox: "Point" on slide 3 (316,505), "3." on slide 3
# (675,505), "distinct" on slide 2 (445,505). Grey above the slide, (602,150), only moves
# focus to the PDF view.
#
# Every shot says the page entry ("N / 8") and the slide on screen. A highlight is
# "translucent blue" for a selection and "yellow" (orange for the current match) for find.
wait 3

# Focus the PDF view. Nothing is selected or highlighted.
click 602 150
wait 1

# Start: slide 1 of 8 in Single Page, entry "1 / 8". Nothing is highlighted.
shot start-slide-1

key Right
wait 1

# Right goes to slide 2: "Slide 2" and "Point bravo" centred, entry "2 / 8". Nothing
# is highlighted.
shot slide-2

# Double-click "distinct" on slide 2: only "distinct" in the body line is highlighted,
# entry "2 / 8". This selection sets the clipboard before the Ctrl+C check on slide 4
# below, so that check cannot pass on a stale clipboard.
dblclick 445 505
wait 1
shot slide-2-word-selected

key ctrl+c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m10.4/clipcheck word-distinct

key Right
wait 1

# Right goes to slide 3: "Slide 3" and "Point charlie" centred, entry "3 / 8". The
# slide 2 selection belongs to slide 2, so nothing is highlighted here.
shot slide-3-no-slide-2-highlight

# Drag from "Point" to "3." on slide 3 selects the whole body line. Only "Point charlie:
# distinct body text for slide 3." is highlighted, translucent blue over each word, and
# the "Slide 3" heading is not. Entry "3 / 8".
drag 316 505 675 505
wait 1
shot slide-3-selected

key Right
wait 1

# Right goes to slide 4: "Slide 4" and "Point delta" centred, entry "4 / 8". No
# highlight anywhere: the selection belongs to slide 3.
shot slide-4-no-highlight

# Ctrl+C on slide 4 copies the slide 3 selection. The clipboard was "distinct" before
# this copy, so the check fails unless the copy takes the slide 3 text.
key ctrl+c
wait 1
run /tmp/agentic-reader-m10.4/clipcheck slide-3-line-from-slide-4

key Left
wait 1

# Left goes back to slide 3: "Slide 3" and "Point charlie" centred, entry "3 / 8". The
# highlight on "Point charlie: distinct body text for slide 3." is back, the same as
# slide-3-selected.
shot slide-3-highlight-kept

# Home goes to slide 1, entry "1 / 8". Nothing is highlighted.
key Home
wait 1

key ctrl+f
type delta
wait 1

# Enter after typing "delta" (on slide 4 only): slide 4 shown, "Slide 4" and "Point delta"
# centred, entry "4 / 8". "delta" in the body line is orange (the current match) and the
# count reads "1 of 1". Nothing on slide 1 is highlighted. The pane is shifted down by the
# bar's height.
key Return
wait 1
shot find-delta-enter-flips-to-slide-4

# Escape closes the find bar. Click the grey above the slide to focus the PDF view, then
# Home goes to slide 1. Entry "1 / 8". No find highlight and no selection highlight.
key Escape
wait 1
click 602 150
key Home
wait 1

key ctrl+f
key ctrl+a
type distinct
wait 1

# "distinct" is on all 8 slides. The first match is on slide 1, so the slide shown is
# slide 1 with the count "1 of 8": "distinct" in "Point alpha: distinct body text for
# slide 1." is orange, and no other highlight. Entry "1 / 8".
shot distinct-slide-1-first-match

key Return
wait 1

# Enter goes to the next match: slide 2, "Point bravo" line with "distinct" orange,
# count "2 of 8", entry "2 / 8". Nothing on slide 1 is highlighted.
shot enter-slide-2

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: slide 3, count "3 of 8", entry "3 / 8", "distinct" orange on its body line.
shot enter-slide-3

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: slide 4, count "4 of 8", entry "4 / 8", "distinct" orange on its body line.
shot enter-slide-4

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: slide 5, count "5 of 8", entry "5 / 8", "distinct" orange on its body line.
shot enter-slide-5

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: slide 6, count "6 of 8", entry "6 / 8", "distinct" orange on its body line.
shot enter-slide-6

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: slide 7, count "7 of 8", entry "7 / 8", "distinct" orange on its body line.
shot enter-slide-7

key Return
wait 1

# Enter: slide 8, count "8 of 8", entry "8 / 8", "distinct" orange on its body line.
shot enter-slide-8

key Return
wait 1

# Enter on the last match wraps to the first: slide 1, count "1 of 8", entry "1 / 8",
# "distinct" orange on the body line of slide 1.
shot enter-wraps-to-slide-1

key shift+Return
wait 1

# Shift+Enter on the first match wraps to the last: slide 8, count "8 of 8", entry
# "8 / 8", "distinct" orange on its body line.
shot shift-enter-wraps-to-slide-8

key shift+Return
wait 1

# Shift+Enter goes back one match: slide 7, count "7 of 8", entry "7 / 8", "distinct"
# orange on its body line.
shot shift-enter-slide-7

# Continuous regression (M3.3 behaviour, unchanged). Ctrl+Shift+L switches to
# Continuous and keeps slide 7 at the top of the pane. Its body line with "distinct" in
# orange is visible about 240 px below the top of the slide (the slide top at about y 122
# with the bar open). Count "7 of 8", entry "7 / 8". Slide 8 is partly visible below it.
key ctrl+shift+l
wait 2
shot continuous-match-on-slide-7

key Return
wait 1
key Return
wait 2

# Enter twice from "7 of 8": "8 of 8", then wrap to "1 of 8". The view scrolled up to
# slide 1, so its body line with "distinct" in orange is visible in the pane, about 240 px
# below the top of the slide. Count "1 of 8", entry "1 / 8". Slide 7 is not in view.
shot continuous-enter-wraps-scrolls-to-slide-1

key shift+Return
wait 2

# Shift+Enter wraps back to the last match. The view scrolled down so that slide 8's body
# line with "distinct" in orange is visible in the pane. Count "8 of 8", entry "8 / 8".
# Slide 1 is not in view.
shot continuous-shift-enter-wraps-scrolls-to-slide-8
